# Fair CRM development standard is mandatory

Canonical source:
`kyrox-platform/projects/fair-crm/DEVELOPMENT_STANDARD.md`

Before changing product code for a new module, feature, CRUD flow, permission, route, migration, backend behavior or frontend UI:

1. Read the canonical development standard.
2. Complete Gate 0 / Delivery Contract for all applicable fields.
3. Apply ADR-009 ownership and Tier classification rules.
4. Decide permission scope for every new permission before implementation.
5. Follow the gate order; do not jump directly from request to API/page code.
6. Backend truth, tenant isolation and authorization must exist before UI is accepted.
7. UI navigation, routes and actions must reflect effective permissions; backend authorization remains mandatory.
8. Real JWT + organization + Core authorization + Fair CRM API + UI acceptance is required for permission-sensitive work. Mock/bypass/build-only evidence is insufficient.
9. Frontend UI changes also require `kyrox-platform/projects/fair-crm/frontend/FRONTEND_UI_MASTER_STANDARD.md`.
10. Permission changes also require `kyrox-platform/projects/fair-crm/PERMISSION_SCOPE_GOVERNANCE.md`.

Hard stop conditions include ambiguous requirements, guessed permission scope, missing tenant scoping, hard-coded authenticated organization IDs, missing route/action permission guards, duplicated UI primitives, stale-runtime acceptance, or unintended real-runtime 401/403/500.

Do not duplicate the canonical Markdown standard inside this repository. Update `kyrox-platform` when the rule changes.
